[h1]Sea Power Tactical UI[/h1]
A tactical interface layer for Sea Power that takes routine micromanagement off your hands: ASW and air-defence patrols, torpedo evasion, radar coverage, contact info and intercept courses.

[h2]Features[/h2]
[b]Anti-submarine warfare[/b]
[list]
[*] The "Aviation: ASW / SAR" window drives helicopter and aircraft ASW groups: search along a course, search in an area, "Corridor" (rows of buoys on both sides of the course) and "Barrier" (a sliding strip of several lines across the course).
[*] When an air threat gets close, ASW, SAR and strike aircraft retreat under cover of your ships. Air-defence fighters do not retreat: they stay in the fight.
[*] SAR for ships, submarines and aircraft: rescue radius, one or a group, a raft is kept by one rescuer.
[/list]

[b]Air defence[/b]
[list]
[*] The "Air defence" (CAP) window: a group, a zone on the map, N aircraft in the zone and K ready on deck. Patrol size follows the range of the missiles.
[*] "Stand-by" mode: the group waits on deck and launches against an incoming raid. The mod orders sorties and swaps aircraft by missiles and fuel.
[*] Search radar of an aircraft is switched on for the task and restored afterwards (never touched if you switched it off).
[/list]

[b]Aircraft: "After launch"[/b]
[list]
[*] A mode for self-homing missiles (IR, active radar, anti-radiation): after the launch the aircraft does not keep guiding the missile but breaks away at once. With "Break away, next target" it then picks the next target.
[*] Set it in the game's own Standing Orders window (all units, group or single aircraft) or in the radial menu. Missiles that need the target illuminated are left alone.
[/list]

[b]Submarine: smart attack[/b]
[list]
[*] Radial menu of a submarine, sector NW, then click the target on the map or in 3D. The torpedo approaches the target from the side, and neutrals near the target are checked. Cancel with sector W.
[/list]

[b]Torpedo evasion and anti-torpedo rockets[/b]
[list]
[*] Own evasion: anti-submarine rocket launchers (RBU) fire first at the incoming tracks, then the ship turns away. Neighbours without a threat cover the targeted ones.
[*] Can be turned off; the game's native evasion is selectable in Settings.
[/list]

[b]Radar layer and jamming[/b]
[list]
[*] A map layer shows what your radars really see, with jamming taken into account and a legend on the map.
[/list]

[b]Range rings and intercept[/b]
[list]
[*] Range rings for the weapons you tick: for your own unit (XO menu) or for an identified enemy (Ctrl + right click).
[*] Intercept course: Ctrl + right click on a contact gives the time and course from the track data you have; the route avoids land.
[/list]

[b]Overview, task line, radial menu, settings[/b]
[list]
[*] "Overview": the "Contacts" tab and the "Own" tab (ships, submarines and aircraft in the air with task, depth/altitude, speed, loadout and group). Click a row to select the unit and centre the map.
[*] The "Task:" line of the bottom panel shows what the mod is doing now ("ASW Barrier: to line 1/2", "Patrol: on station", "Stand-by: intercepting raid", "Torpedo evasion").
[*] Radial command ring (hold the left mouse button on a unit): torpedo alert, break away, cease fire, return control, smart attack, return to base, return to formation.
[*] Contact info labels from your own sensors only: depth, speed, CPA/TCPA, track age, noise.
[*] "Settings" window in a mission: keys, languages (English, Russian, Chinese — the Chinese text is a machine translation, corrections welcome), performance, all of the config without editing files.
[/list]

[h2]Requirements[/h2]
As for any DLL mod of Sea Power: install the AnchorChain loader once. Download [b]ACPreloader.zip[/b] (BepInEx is included) and extract it into the game folder, next to [i]Sea Power.exe[/i] — see the [url=https://seapower-modders.github.io/AnchorChain/install-anchor-chain.html]AnchorChain install guide[/url]. AnchorChain itself is a Required item and comes from the Workshop together with this mod.

Also copy [i]SeaPowerTacticalUI.Loader.dll[/i] from the [i]loader[/i] folder of the item ([i]Steam\steamapps\workshop\content\1286220\3827955062\loader[/i]) into [i]Sea Power\BepInEx\plugins[/i]. If the mod has already run on your PC, it put the file there itself.

